&lt;h2&gt;


  Free to use
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Planela is currently &lt;strong&gt;completely free with no limits&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No restrictions on players, sessions, or features.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want to try it with your team:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://planela.io" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://planela.io&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Feedback is very welcome, especially from teams that run sprint planning regularly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;April 6, 2026. That's the date.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you're a self-employed developer in the UK earning over £50k, Making Tax Digital for Income Tax kicks in. Quarterly digital submissions to HMRC. Compatible software mandatory. Paper records no longer accepted.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;And based on every conversation I've had? Almost nobody's actually ready.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What's actually changing
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Quarterly updates&lt;/strong&gt; — submit income/expense summaries to HMRC every 3 months via compatible software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Digital records&lt;/strong&gt; — spreadsheets count (if they meet the standard), but notebooks don't&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;End of Period Statement&lt;/strong&gt; — annual summary replacing your current tax return process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Final Declaration&lt;/strong&gt; — replaces the self-assessment tax return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why developers specifically should care
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Because loads of us hit £50k. Contract rates in the UK have been strong. And unlike employed developers who have payroll handling everything, we're doing this ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The threshold drops to £30k in April 2027. If you're anywhere near either number, this affects you.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What you actually need to do (in order)
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Check if you're affected&lt;/strong&gt; — &lt;a href="https://landolio.com/tools/mtd-readiness-checker" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MTD readiness checker&lt;/a&gt; (2 minutes, tells you exactly where you stand)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Pick compatible software&lt;/strong&gt; — HMRC has an &lt;a href="https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-software-thats-compatible-with-making-tax-digital-for-income-tax" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;approved list&lt;/a&gt;. Free Spreadsheets work IF they connect via bridging software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Set up digital record keeping&lt;/strong&gt; — start now, don't wait for April&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Understand the penalty system&lt;/strong&gt; — it's points-based now. &lt;a href="https://landolio.com/tools/mtd-penalty-calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Calculate your risk&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Budget for it&lt;/strong&gt; — &lt;a href="https://landolio.com/tools/mtd-cost-calculator" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;estimate your compliance costs&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The penalties are real
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;New points-based system:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1 point per late quarterly submission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hit the threshold (4 points) → £200 penalty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Points only reset after 24 months of compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is stricter than self-assessment. They're not messing about.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  The honest truth
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MTD is going to be annoying for the first year. Extra admin, new software, quarterly instead of annual.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But once you're in the groove? Having up-to-date records quarterly actually makes the annual process &lt;em&gt;easier&lt;/em&gt;. No more January panic scrambling for receipts from April.&lt;/p&gt;

